+// SIM_SetSpriteDepthBias: polygons drawn while it is set are moved toward the camera for the depth test only (their
+// place on screen is unchanged), by nothing at their lowest point on screen up to `top` (fx32, in view units) at their
+// highest. A standing sprite's head then clears what stands just behind it (a sign's lower edge) while its feet stay
+// where the ground's effects (tall grass) can cover them. The DS snaps polygon edges to its 256x192 pixels, which
+// hides most of those overlaps; drawn at a higher resolution they show
+static fx32 s_spriteDepthBiasTop;
+
+extern "C" void SIM_SetSpriteDepthBias(fx32 top)
+{
+    s_spriteDepthBiasTop = top;
+}
